{
  "about": "Shared attachment grammar fixture (Spec #123 R3, R4, R33; WI #134 owns it, ruling D18). The Rust core (crates/memex-core/tests/attachments_grammar.rs) and the app's Dart mirror read every row. references: `markdown` is the whole string given to the parser; when `valid`, `kind` is image or link, `path` is the percent-decoded vault-relative path and `name` the decoded name; otherwise kind, path and name are null. encode: the markdown for a stored `name` of content `hash`, its `kind`, and `encoded_name` (the percent-encoded name in the URL). executable: whether a file of that `name` is revealed, never opened (R33's table, last extension, any letter case; the executable-bit rule is tested on real files).",
  "hash": "66bc7611813b7443f25c4af21004864b3975eb83fb7c74be572b9d6aa74bd462",
